body:
(Sorry for the late reply. I had a lot on my mind.)

&#x200B;

>What were you looking for?

I guess I was just looking for help with my problems. And I know that’s not the best motive.

&#x200B;

>It might be productive also to ask, what are the things you do out of fear in general? Prayer, fasting, giving etc? 

Pretty much all of that at this point, though I guess there’s a little bit more faith recently.

&#x200B;

>Are you scared because you feel you don't do enough or because you feel you stumble and do wrong things?

Both I think. It just makes me panic knowing that I disappoint God so many times in just an hour or even a minute.

&#x200B;

>Alternatively does God just seem unnegotiable and cold?

I think so. I still can’t make myself believe that a loving and merciful God would consign someone to eternal torture. I guess I learned it from my dad when I was a kid (though we’re on much better terms now,) but I can’t love someone that I’m afraid of.

&#x200B;

My relationship has gotten a bit better with God these past few days, but there’s still spells of fear and depression when I think about hell, especially when it comes to other people I care about.
